<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Second Polish Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1939 CE · capital Warsaw</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent interwar Poland, reborn in 1918 after 123 years of partition, which defeated the Red Army in 1920 and fell to Germany and the USSR in 1939.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As the partitioning empires collapsed in November 1918, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jozef-pilsudski">Jozef Pilsudski</a> took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regency-council-kingdom-of-poland">Regency Council</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1916-1918">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1916-1918), and independence was proclaimed on 11 November. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland's</a> borders were settled by war: with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-ukrainian-peoples-republic">West Ukrainian People's Republic</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-greater-poland">Greater Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>, and with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>, whose army was defeated at Warsaw in 1920.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution of 1921 created a parliamentary republic, but after President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-narutowicz">Gabriel Narutowicz</a> was murdered in 1922 and governments proved unstable, Pilsudski seized power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-poland">May Coup</a> of 1926. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanation">Sanation</a> regime ruled until 1939. About a third of the population were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukrainians">Ukrainians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarusians">Belarusians</a> and Germans. The state built the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gdynia">Gdynia</a> and the Central Industrial District.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany</a> invaded on 1 September 1939 and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> on 17 September, dividing the country. The government went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> was re-established in 1945 with new borders under communist rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/second-polish-republic.jpg" alt="Second Polish Republic" width="320" height="201"><figcaption>Image: Arvedui89 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Poland_(1928%E2%80%931980).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1939 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Warsaw</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jozef Pilsudski, Gabriel Narutowicz, Ignacy Moscicki</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a>, <a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/belarus">Belarus</a>, <a href="/countries/lithuania">Lithuania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Poland (1918-1939), Interwar Poland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=second-polish-republic" aria-label="Second Polish Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5153 374 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second Polish Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5473 630L5473 630M5473 630L5300 622M5473 630L5820 533M5473 630L5472 631M5473 630L5494 677M5473 630L5482 707M5473 630L5508 714M5473 630L5556 562M5473 630L5556 562M5473 630L5551 699"/>